    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on integrating a payment gateway via a REST API and im getting stuck. i keep getting a 402 Payment Required error in the json response, but i've checked the card details and they seem fine. what are the usual reasons for this error and how should i go about debugging the payload to see what's actually wrong?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A 402 Payment Required error usually means the payment processor has rejected the transaction, even if your card details look correct. Common causes include insufficient funds, an expired card, or blockages by the issuing bank's fraud detection system. To debug your payload, carefully inspect the API documentation for required fields, check if all mandatory data types are correct, and log the raw request body you are sending just before the call.",
